  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-04-19T03:53:32.202Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, as a creator the approval process of getting a world public (out of labs) seems far too difficult with the growing number of players and creators on VRChat. This especially applies if you are not a relevant/popular creator to begin with.\nHowever, my biggest issue with the current Community Labs situation is the lack of attention older worlds get. Once a world is uploaded, you have an extremely limited and small window of time (usually a few hours) to get your worlds name out there before more new community worlds show up further pushing your world away from the top of the list. This slows down visits significantly and makes it nearly impossible for anyone to visit your world again.\nWhat I propose here is the idea of adding more community labs categories rather than just displaying new community worlds. Maybe a way to search for community worlds and some category that displays recently updated community worlds would improve the situation for many creators here.",
